// PORT-PENDING 0640 crates-jet-pkg-model-src-prelude-plugin-module-group: crates/jet-pkg-model/src/Prelude/Plugin.rs:1-1817
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS // core.plugin runtime (D-DEP-WASM1=A, c81) — sandboxed WASM Component Model
//RS // plugin loader, via wasmtime's dynamic component API.
//RS //
//RS // This file is emitted verbatim into the hidden FFI bridge crate (see
//RS // Source/FFI.rs) when a Jet program uses `core.plugin`. The compiler crate
//RS // (`Source/`) never depends on `wasmtime`; it only ships this text. Owner-
//RS // approved I6 bootstrap exception (D-DEP-WASM1=A): wasmtime + the Component
//RS // Model is the plugin sandbox engine, runtime-side only.
//RS //
//RS // Host import admission is checked against typed HostImportFacts and the one
//RS // canonical Authority lent at load time. Every import is preflighted before
//RS // linker instantiation; an unregistered or denied import cannot reach an
//RS // external adapter. Every file read uses a resource-scoped, no-follow FS.Read
//RS // root. A plugin with no declared/imported capability still runs with a
//RS // zero-grant scope (I1).
//RS //
//RS // Handles and stores are owner-thread state in a thread-local HashMap,
//RS // mirroring `DB.rs`. Handle 0 is the error sentinel (never a live plugin
//RS // instance). Nested host/guest entry and unload during a call are rejected,
//RS // so a guest failure cannot unwind unrelated host work.
//RS //
//RS // Wire protocol (mirrors `DB.rs`'s tagged-length encoding for leaves and uses
//RS // canonical recursive component values for aggregates):
//RS // `I<len>:<int>`, `F<len>:<float>`, `B<len>:<true|false>`, `T<len>:<utf8>`,
//RS // `L<count>:<values>`, `R<count>:<field-name><value>`, `Q<count>:<values>`,
//RS // `N`/`P<value>` for none/some, `K`/`X<value>` for ok/error, `V<case><value>`
//RS // for variants, `E<len>:<case>` for enums, and `G<count>:<flag-names>` for
//RS // flags. A call result or error is `O:<value>` / `E:<kind>:<message>`. The
//RS // wire is only a transport envelope; values are checked against the actual
//RS // Component Model `Type` before every call and after every return. Failure
//RS // kinds are user error, denied authority, budget exhaustion, and internal
//RS // defect; classification uses typed boundary state, never backend strings.
//RS 
